      "summary": "The implementation covers the requested identity, telemetry, and alert behavior, but the Terraform tests miss two explicit regression checks: widened app grant scopes and alerts routed away from the configured owner.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "infra/terraform/tests/identity-telemetry.tftest.hcl",
          "line": 60,
          "message": "M-14's tests do not detect widened scopes on the OpenAI or telemetry grants.",
          "confidence": 0.94,
          "category": "testing",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The M-14 tests assert the evidence assignment's exact scope, but check only role names and principal types for the OpenAI and telemetry assignments. They do not reject app assignments at subscription or resource-group scope.",
            "failureScenario": "If the OpenAI or telemetry assignment is widened to resource-group scope, the current assertions still pass. The issue's M-14 criterion and scope notes require widened grants to be detected."
          }
        },
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "infra/terraform/tests/identity-telemetry.tftest.hcl",
          "line": 270,
          "message": "M-15's test does not verify that every alert routes to the configured owner's action group.",
          "confidence": 0.93,
          "category": "testing",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The M-15 test checks that every alert has one action group and separately checks the configured owner's receiver, but never compares each alert's action group ID with the owner's action group ID.",
            "failureScenario": "If an alert is changed to route to a different action group, the assertions still pass while the configured owner receives no alert."
          }
        }
